Subject: [PATCH] CMake: Report 1.1.1 as the project version

The 1.1.1 release never bumped project(VERSION), which is still 1.1.0 from
the previous release.  Everything derived from it inherits the stale number:
libunarr.pc says "Version: 1.1.0" and unarr-version.cmake sets
PACKAGE_VERSION to 1.1.0, so pkg-config --atleast-version=1.1.1 and
find_package(unarr 1.1.1) both fail against a full 1.1.1 install.  The
shared library's VERSION/SOVERSION come from the same variable.

Upstream reworked versioning wholesale after this release (commit d8c9daa33,
"Refactor versioning", unreleased) rather than fixing the number in place,
so there is no commit to backport -- drop this on the next version bump and
check that the new release got its own version right.

Upstream: not submitted (fixed differently on master, after 1.1.1)
Applies-to: all environments
---
diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index bdb7885..60c9650 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@ cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.16...4.0 FATAL_ERROR)
 
 project(
   unarr
-  VERSION 1.1.0
+  VERSION 1.1.1
   LANGUAGES C)
 set(PROJECT_DESCRIPTION "A decompression library for rar, tar and zip files.")
 
